# Dated source backups created by the assistant's edit workflow.
# These are local safety nets and must never be committed.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.bak2-*
*.bak3-*
*.bak*

# Build artifacts
*.o
src/*.o
src/wais/*.o
src/libwww/*.o
MGT_Unicorn_Suite_x64.exe

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-08-02, when the project was first placed under git.
#
# Rules that could hide a real build input are ANCHORED to the project
# root with a leading slash. The loose files at the root are almost all
# verification output; the same extensions inside logos/, icons/,
# assets/, docs/ and test/ are genuine inputs and stay tracked. That is
# why these are not blanket patterns.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Reconstructed files, should any ever be written. Kept distinct from
# *.bak precisely because a reconstruction is not a preserved copy.
*.reconstructed-*

# Dated snapshots of source and executables under names the *.bak rules
# above do not match, for example
# suite_shell.c.20260625T222002Z-known-good-pre-terminal-rename
/backups/

# Built release payload, regenerated by the packaging step
/_release_0.3.1/

# Compiler and linker output
*.obj
*.res
*.map
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exe

# Executable snapshots whose suffix comes AFTER the .exe, so neither
# *.exe nor *.bak matches them, for example
# MGT_Unicorn_Suite_x64.exe.RELEASE-table-engine-20260717T212621Z
*.exe.*

# Build and verification logs
*.log
*.err
*.log.utf8
*.log.prev

# Packaging archive. Anchored: docs/MGTWAIS.ZIP is documentation and
# must stay tracked.
/*.zip
/*.ZIP

# Verification screenshots, render output and captured wire streams.
# Anchored: docs/*.png, icons/*.png and logos/*.png are build inputs and
# reference material.
/*.png
/*.bmp
/*.wav
/rip_capture*.bin
/rip_probe*.bin
/ripscrip_ours.*

# Debris from a verification script whose helper function name collided
# with the New-Item alias, leaving 462 empty files named after pixel
# colours. Ignored rather than deleted; see the housekeeping report.
/Color \[A=*

# Claude Code project settings. Local tool configuration rather than
# project source, and it carries a permission mode that should not be
# inherited by anyone who later gets a copy of this repository.
/.claude/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored WebView2 SDK, pruned to the headers the build actually uses.
#
# build_x64.bat passes -Ithird_party\webview2\build\native\include and
# nothing else, LDFLAGS links no webview2 library, and the runtime
# loader is the root WebView2Loader.dll reached through LoadLibrary. So
# the static libs, the nupkg, the runtimes, the managed assemblies and
# the tools are 52 MB the build never reads.
#
# Ignore everything under the SDK, then negate back the include
# directory. Git does not descend into an ignored directory, so each
# parent on the path has to be un-ignored first or the negation for the
# headers can never be reached.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
/third_party/*
!/third_party/webview2/
/third_party/webview2/*
!/third_party/webview2/build/
/third_party/webview2/build/*
!/third_party/webview2/build/native/
/third_party/webview2/build/native/*
!/third_party/webview2/build/native/include/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-08-02, Phase 4 Zmodem receive.
#
# The Zmodem core is different in kind from the WebView2 SDK above. It
# is small, it is a build input the link step names directly, and it is
# MODIFIED: two GPL files were removed and replaced. A modified vendored
# core that is not in the repository cannot be audited or rebuilt, so
# this one is tracked. Its object files are not.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
!/third_party/mbzm/
/third_party/mbzm/*.o

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-08-02, MSI packaging. The WiX source and the build script
# are tracked; what they GENERATE is not. installer/payload is a staged
# copy of files that already live in the repository, and installer/out
# holds the built MSI.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
/installer/payload/
/installer/out/
# installer/art is regenerated from assets by tools/gen_installer_art.py
/installer/art/
*.wixpdb
tools/__pycache__/
